  "body": "## Goal\n\nUse one explicitly selected closed DXF chain of straight segments as a source for the existing vertical Wire Contour operation. A sketch can contain other chains. Reuse the existing stable chain selection, stock placement, wire generator and verification on main.\n\nThis is an independently usable part of #2022. #2978 covers a whole-sketch native punch in a draft. #3178 covers the separate native post for reentrant curved openings.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nSelect a single closed chain through the normal source selection. Post a supported synthetic through-cut with stock, a valid explicit start, side and holding settings. Compare the posted path with the existing generator on equivalent model geometry. The other sketch loops must not enter the program.\n\nPreserve source selection, placement and direction on save and reopen. Invalidate the result when the referenced source or its setup changes. Refuse missing or stale selectors, open or ambiguous chains, unqualified overlaps and arcs with a diagnostic. Keep the arc data available to later qualified consumers. Do not flatten curves or fall back to the full sketch.\n\nSuggested labels: enhancement, P6, effort:high, area:2d, area:post, source:agent.\n",
